---
/* Ported from docs/preview/colors-theme-dark.html (CCWEB2-317 phase 2).
 *
 * Nothing but the shell was extracted — this page has no repeated structure to
 * collapse. The five surface steps look like a candidate and are not: each
 * carries different prose, and the whole point of the demo is that a reader can
 * read the five hexes in source order next to the fills they produce.
 */
import DocPage from '../../layouts/DocPage.astro';
---
<DocPage
  title="CODECAVE — The dark canvas (the only theme)"
  nav="foundations"
  stylesheets={['preview.css']}
>
<style slot="head" is:inline>
  .stack-demo { border-radius: var(--radius-card); overflow: hidden;
                border: 1px solid var(--color-surface-quaternary); }
  .stack-demo > div { padding: 1.5rem; font-size: var(--text-caption);
                      font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--color-body-secondary-lighter); }
  .fg-row { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem 0;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-surface-quaternary); }
  .fg-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .fg-row .sample { flex: 1; min-width: 14rem; }
</style>

<div class="pv-shell">
  <a class="pv-back" href="index.html">&larr; All foundations</a>

  <header class="pv-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Color · card 2 of 3</span>
    <h1>The dark canvas — CODECAVE&rsquo;s only theme</h1>
    <p>The defining decision of the system: the page and its cards sit one barely-perceptible step
       apart. Depth is carried by radius, border and the upward glow — never by lightening a
       surface. Check the four steps below read as <em>separate</em> without reading as
       <em>contrasted</em>.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>The four surface steps</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">Total luminance spread across all four is smaller than a single step in most
       dark UI kits. That is intentional and must survive review.</p>
    <div class="stack-demo">
      <div style="background:var(--color-surface-primary)">--color-surface-primary · #0A0A0B · the page</div>
      <div style="background:var(--color-surface-secondary)">--color-surface-secondary · #0F0F15 · card fill (one step off the page)</div>
      <div style="background:var(--color-surface-tertiary)">--color-surface-tertiary · #1C1C27 · raised / hovered card, icon tiles</div>
      <div style="background:var(--color-surface-primary-hover)">--color-surface-primary-hover · #232339 · surface hover</div>
      <div style="background:var(--color-surface-quaternary)">--color-surface-quaternary · #2B2848 · borders, dividers, checkbox outline</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>Foreground ramp on the page</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">Three text weights of grey, each with a defined job. Nothing dimmer than
       <code>#9595BB</code> is permitted for text that carries meaning.</p>
    <div class="pv-tile" style="background:var(--color-surface-primary)">
      <div class="fg-row">
        <span class="sample" style="color:var(--color-heading);font-size:var(--text-subhead);font-weight:700">Optimize costs. Protect your Data</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">--color-heading · #F4F4F6<br>headings · 18.0:1</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fg-row">
        <span class="sample" style="color:var(--color-body-primary)">We scope, price and warranty the work before it starts.</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">--color-body-primary · #F4F4F6<br>body · 18.0:1</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fg-row">
        <span class="sample" style="color:var(--color-body-secondary-lighter)">Long-form description copy sits one step down, so a paragraph never competes with the heading above it.</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">--color-body-secondary-lighter · #C7C7DB<br>descriptions · 11.9:1</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fg-row">
        <span class="sample" style="color:var(--color-body-secondary);font-size:var(--text-caption)">14 Aug 2026 · 6 min read</span>
        <span class="pv-meta">--color-body-secondary · #9595BB<br>metadata &amp; placeholders only · 6.87:1<br><strong>a role rule — long-form copy uses the lighter steps</strong></span>
      </div>
      <div class="fg-row">
        <a class="sample" href="#" style="font-weight:700">Discuss project for free</a>
        <span class="pv-meta">--color-action &rarr; --color-hovered on hover<br>hover raises contrast, never lowers it</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <h2>In situ — page, card, raised card</h2>
    <p class="pv-note">The same content at three surface levels. Confirm separation comes from
       corner radius and the 1px border, not from fill.</p>
    <div class="pv-grid pv-grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="font-size:var(--text-caption)">Cloud &amp; DevOps</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:var(--text-subhead);line-height:var(--leading-subhead);margin:0.5rem 0 0.75rem">Optimize costs.<br>Protect your Data</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--color-body-secondary-lighter);font-size:var(--text-caption);margin:0 0 1.5rem">
          Default card: <code>#0F0F15</code> fill, 24px radius, 1px <code>#2B2848</code> border,
          padding <code>32px 32px 48px</code>.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-tertiary" href="#">Learn more</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="background:var(--color-surface-tertiary)">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="font-size:var(--text-caption)">Autodesk plugins</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:var(--text-subhead);line-height:var(--leading-subhead);margin:0.5rem 0 0.75rem">10x efficiency with<br>custom Plugins</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--color-body-secondary-lighter);font-size:var(--text-caption);margin:0 0 1.5rem">
          Raised / hovered card: <code>#1C1C27</code>. This is the entire hover delta for a card —
          nothing scales, nothing brightens.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-tertiary" href="#">Learn more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pv-block">
    <p class="pv-warn"><strong>There is no light theme.</strong> The system ships none, and one must
      not be derived. The three light-surface exceptions are catalogued in
      <a href="colors-theme-light.html">colors-theme-light.html</a>.</p>
  </section>
</div>

</DocPage>
